  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nIssued 110 AM MDT FRI AUG 7 2026\nFollowing the passage of the weak disturbance in the short-term,\nflow aloft will take on a zonal posture with the high pressure\naloft shifting to our south. Temperatures on Monday will cool \nto near normal, where they will hover throughout the rest of the\nperiod. Each afternoon will also feature breezy conditions. \nUncertainty in the pattern evolution begins to increase come \nmid-week this coming week. The LREF grand ensemble indicates \ntroughing developing over the Pacific Northwest come midweek and\nbeyond, with another push of monsoonal moisture making it's way\nnorth. For now the long-term forecast is dry, but the monsoonal\npush will be monitored for the potential need to introduce \nprecip and thunder chances as the pattern evolution comes into \nbetter focus.",
